export const meta = { name: 'factorio-writer-U', description: 'FACTORIO-01 сводчик ветви U (без предела длины)', phases: [{ title: 'Свод' }] }
const P = "Ты сводишь правила для агентов, которые строят полностью автоматические заводы в Factorio (среда FLE, Python-инструменты). Ниже — весь опыт команды: три свода правил, которые написали три независимые линии, и все эпизоды, по которым они писались (что построили, какие уроки записали и что показала игра: выпуск после 45 игровых минут без агента, когда ручные запасы убраны). Не открывай никаких файлов и не запускай код — работай только по тексту ниже.\n\nСвод S1:\n-----\nСВОД ПРАВИЛ: автоматические заводы в FLE\n\nАрхитектура и питание\n1. Строй полностью электрический завод: электробуры, электропечи, AM2, питание от пара. Углём снабжай только бойлер. [iron_plate, gear, circuit, inserter, sci1, logistics: громоздкая топливная логистика]\n2. Самое простое питание бойлера: поставь электробур на край угольного поля, затем place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, side, spacing=0). Бур сыплет уголь прямо в бойлер, без лент и инсертеров. Проверь, что drop_position попадает внутрь бойлера. Если так не выходит: 2 угольных бура → прямая лента → burner-инсертер → бойлер. С последней клетки одной ленты можно кормить два бойлера, поставив инсертеры с разных сторон. [iron_plate, circuit, gear, inserter, logistics: дедлок «нет угля → нет тока»]\n3. Burner-инсертер держит в бойлере около 5 угля, это норма. О снабжении суди по тому, держится ли уровень со временем. На последнем шаге забей бойлер до 50 угля: это запас на сброс. [inserter, sci1, logistics, gear: ложная тревога, остановка после сброса]\n4. Считай мощность при полной нагрузке. Паровой двигатель даёт 900 кВт. Потребление: печь 180, AM2 150, бур 90 кВт. 1,8 МВт хватает примерно на 15 машин, но 27 машин дают LOW_POWER. Не хватает двигателей — скрафти их через craft_item (8 шестерён, 10 пластин, 5 труб), взяв пластины из своих печей. Второй двигатель ставь place_entity_next_to(SteamEngine, eng.position, dir, spacing=0). [logistics, inserter, sci1, gear: просадка питания]\n5. Ориентиры: 2 бура на одну электропечь (3x3) дают около 37 пластин в минуту, и узким местом становится печь. Бур даёт около 30 руды в минуту. Закладывай двукратный запас над квотой. Замеры на шагах — только подсказка. [iron_plate, gear, circuit, logistics: переоценка выпуска]\n6. Где можно, соединяй машины напрямую: печь → инсертер → AM2 → инсертер → AM2 → сундук. Промежуточная лента не нужна. Обычный инсертер переносит около 50 предметов в минуту, поэтому на быстрые звенья ставь два. [circuit, inserter, sci1: лишние ленты, узкие звенья]\n\nРазмещение\n7. Ленты клади поклеточно, прямыми участками, через place_entity(TransportBelt, pos, dir). Ошибки собирай в список. connect_entities для лент оставляет разрывы и затирает существующие ленты. Через connect_entities надёжно строятся только трубы по ровной земле (около 25 клеток). [gear, sci1, logistics, iron_plate]\n8. Раскладку заранее расчерти в фиксированных координатах. Строй крупным блоком через хелпер P(proto, x, y, dir), который делает move_to и try/except и копит исключения. В каждом цикле используй свою переменную, не переиспользуй x, иначе сущности уедут. [inserter, sci1, logistics: ошибки при постройке по частям, сдвиг координат]\n9. direction инсертера — сторона выгрузки, direction ленты — направление движения. Буры направляй на ленту или печь. [gear, circuit, inserter: развёрнутые инсертеры]\n10. Средний столб покрывает 7x7. connect_entities для столбов на 60 клеток работает, но машины на краю зоны остаются с NO_POWER, а обход воды может дать отдельную сеть с voltage=0. При обходе ставь столбы вручную каждые 7–8 клеток. [iron_plate, gear, circuit: обесточенные машины]\n11. Воду на маршруте ни can_place_entity, ни nearest не показывают. Перед длинной трассой смотри get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, pos).bounding_box. Обходи углами или сайдлоадом в параллельную ленту, брошенные клетки снимай. [inserter, logistics, circuit: трассы, упирающиеся в воду]\n12. Два продукта на одной ленте разводи по полосам: один подавай инсертером (он кладёт на дальнюю полосу), другой — сайдлоадом с ближней стороны. [logistics, inserter: взаимная блокировка]\n13. Если бойлер повёрнут UP, вода входит с коротких торцов, а длинная сторона свободна под инсертер и ленту. [gear: конфликт труб и подачи]\n\nПроверки и API\n14. Возвращаемый объект и drop_position бывают устаревшими, а place_entity иногда ставит сущность не туда. После каждого блока перечитывай get_entities с позициями и статусами, лишнее чини. [gear, logistics, sci1: координаты от прошлой сущности]\n15. После постройки проверь каждую сущность на NO_POWER и LOW_POWER, а у генераторов — voltage. Статус NOT_CONNECTED у нового двигателя может пройти к следующему шагу. [iron_plate, gear, circuit: ложная или скрытая неисправность]\n16. Фильтр кода запрещает getattr и dunder-имена. Вместо них используй str(type(e)) и 'x' in dir(e). Упавший шаг всё равно засчитывается. Переменные и функции сохраняются между шагами. [gear, circuit, inserter: потерянные шаги]\n17. На каждом шаге проходит 60 с игрового времени. Проверяй узел сразу после постройки, иначе ошибка успеет, например, опустошить бойлер. [gear: бойлер, высохший между шагами]\n-----\n\nСвод S2:\n-----\nСВОД ПРАВИЛ: автоматические заводы в FLE\n\nАРХИТЕКТУРА\n1. Если в инвентаре есть электробуры, электропечи и AM2, стройте полностью электрический завод. [L2p1+L2p2: все 6 задач; лечит: сложную подачу угля к печам]\n2. Котёл ставьте на край угольного поля. Сначала электробур, потом котёл: его клетки должны накрывать drop_position бура (place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, dir) или центр в 3 клетках от бура). Воду ведите через connect_entities(pump, boiler, Pipe), 25 клеток работают. Второй угольный бур с другой стороны даёт запас. Котёл сам держит 50 угля. [L2p2:iron_plate, gear, inserter, automation_science; лечит: остановку энергии без агента и угольные ленты]\n3. Паровые двигатели ставьте direction=UP прямо на steam_output_point котла, второй вплотную за первым (шаг 5 клеток): пар доходит без труб. Если всё же нужна паровая труба, кладите её руками, минимум в клетке от водяных: connect_entities(boiler, engine, Pipe) может прицепиться к водяному входу. [L2p2:gear, electronic_circuit, logistics_science; лечит: двигатель без пара или на воде]\n4. Руду отдавайте без лент: бур → электропечь (3x3) → бур. Центр печи — в 3 клетках от центра бура по его направлению, а не прямо на drop_position, иначе печь упрётся в бур. Такая связка даёт 30–37 пластин/мин, и она обычно и ограничивает выпуск. [L2p1:iron_plate; L2p2:iron_plate, electronic_circuit, inserter; лечит: лишние ленты и коллизии]\n5. Считайте энергию. 1 котёл + 2 двигателя (1,8 МВт) тянут примерно 6–9 буров, 5 печей и 3–4 AM2. Для большего завода нужен второй котёл. Недостающие двигатели можно скрафтить через craft_item из добытой руками руды. [L2p2:logistics_science, automation_science; лечит: LOW_POWER и недобор]\n6. Проектируйте с запасом не меньше 50% над квотой и считайте производительность каждого звена. Базовый манипулятор переносит около 0,83 предмета/с: на быстрые передачи (кабель) ставьте 2–3 штуки. [L2p1:automation_science; L2p2:electronic_circuit, inserter; лечит: недобор квоты]\n7. Полуфабрикаты передавайте манипулятором из сборщика в сборщик. Два продукта разводите по разным лентам или по разным полосам одной ленты (вставка с противоположных сторон, полосы после поворота). [L2p1+L2p2:automation_science, logistics_science; лечит: дедлок смешанной ленты]\n8. Выход собирайте в сундук, лучше двумя манипуляторами. [L2p1:gear; L2p2:gear; лечит: забитый выход]\n\nРАЗМЕЩЕНИЕ\n9. Перед каждой группой построек делайте move_to к цели: дальность place_entity около 10 клеток. В циклах тоже. [L2p2: все задачи; лечит: ошибки \"too far\"]\n10. До прокладки лент и столбов проверьте маршрут и площадку на воду: get_resource_patch(Water, centre, radius) и nearest(Water). can_place_entity вдали от игрока или с предметом не из инвентаря всегда возвращает False, картой он не служит. [L2p2:electronic_circuit, inserter, logistics_science; лечит: потерянные шаги]\n11. Ставьте здания через place_entity с явными координатами и direction=. Направление манипулятора задаёт сторону сброса. Манипулятор у машины 3x3 стоит на соседней с её краем клетке. Печатайте drop_position и проверяйте, что он попадает внутрь клеток цели. [L2p1; L2p2:automation_science, logistics_science; лечит: сброс на землю]\n12. Возвращаемое значение place_entity может оказаться соседней сущностью. Проверяйте результат через get_entities(position=, radius=) с проверкой на None. [L2p1; L2p2:inserter; лечит: работу с чужим объектом]\n13. Ленты кладите вручную, place_entity с направлением. [L2p1:electronic_circuit, logistics_science; лечит: разрывы лент]\n\nЭЛЕКТРОСЕТЬ\n14. connect_entities(MediumElectricPole) на 70–75 клеток строит линию, но оставляет без питания крайние здания и второй двигатель. После sleep ищите NO_POWER и NOT_PLUGGED_IN и добавляйте столбы руками, цепочкой через каждые 7 клеток. [L2p1; L2p2: все 6 задач; лечит: тихо обесточенные здания]\n\nПЕСОЧНИЦА\n15. getattr и import отклоняют весь шаг. get_entities() возвращает и PipeGroup, BeltGroup, ElectricityGroup без warnings, position и voltage: отсеивайте их ('Group' in str(type(e))) до чтения атрибутов. Любое исключение прерывает остаток шага, поэтому рискованные установки оборачивайте в try/except. Переменные присваивайте по одной, без кортежей. [L2p1; L2p2:gear, automation_science, electronic_circuit; лечит: падения цикла и отказы интерпретатора]\n\nПРОВЕРКИ ПЕРЕД ЗАВЕРШЕНИЕМ\n16. Обойдите все сущности и проверьте status. WAITING_FOR_SPACE у угольного бура и 'full' у котла с 50 углём — норма. Убедитесь, что топливо котла не падает. [L2p2:iron_plate, gear, logistics_science; лечит: ложные тревоги и пропущенный голод котла]\n17. Выпуск меряйте как прирост в сундуке за sleep(60), несколько раз подряд. Первый замер завышен запасом пластин (85 против 53). [L2p1:inserter; L2p2:gear, electronic_circuit, inserter; лечит: переоценку выпуска]\n18. Ручные запасы будут убраны. Временные постройки и ручное сырьё не должны входить в схему. Самодостаточность доказывайте измерением. [L2p1, L2p2:logistics_science; лечит: недоказанную самодостаточность]\n-----\n\nСвод S3:\n-----\nСвод правил: автоматические заводы в FLE\n\nСтарт и архитектура\n1. Проверь стартовый инвентарь. Если есть электробуры, электропечи и AM2, делай весь завод электрическим: топливо нужно только котлу. Burner-цепочки без агента встают. [L3p1:iron_plate_throughput, L3p2:все задачи; лечит: остановку после ухода агента]\n2. Сразу запиши координаты ресурсов и воды. nearest() ищет от текущей позиции игрока, поэтому после move_to он может найти другое озеро. Осмотр ресурсов совмещай с первой стройкой. [L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput; лечит: трубы на 75 тайлов и потерянные шаги]\n\nЭнергия\n3. Электростанция: offshore pump → boiler → steam engine. Котёл и двигатель ставь через nearest_buildable с BuildingBox. Насос и котёл соединяй через connect_entities(Pipe), это работает и на 30+ тайлах. Следующий двигатель ставь через place_entity_next_to(spacing=0), пар он подхватит сам. [L3p1, L3p2:iron_plate_throughput, L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput; лечит: неудачную раскладку станции]\n4. Лучший способ подать уголь: котёл прямо в drop_position электробура, через place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, UP). Можно поставить бур с двух сторон. Котёл держит 50 угля. Запасной вариант: бур → лента по одному тайлу → burner-инсертер. Проверь, что последний тайл ленты на месте: range() часто недотягивает на один тайл. [L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput, L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput; лечит: голодание котла]\n5. Считай мощность так, будто все машины работают одновременно. 2 двигателя дают 1.8 МВт; бур берёт 90 кВт, печь 180 кВт, AM2 150 кВт. Если выходит больше, ставь второй котёл (вода через одну трубу со свободного порта первого) и 4 двигателя цепочкой. Для крафта двигателей вручную шестерни не делаются: достань их из AM2 через extract_item, а плиты возьми из печей. [L3p2:inserter_throughput, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput; лечит: LOW_POWER]\n\nПроизводство\n6. В этой версии электропечь занимает 3x3. Ставь её в drop_position бура через place_entity_next_to(drill.position, UP), затем инсертер через place_entity_next_to(furnace.position, UP). Шаг колонки 3 тайла. На одну печь можно направить два бура навстречу. Пара бур+печь даёт ~30 плит/мин. Размеры проверяй через tile_dimensions. [L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:iron_plate_throughput; лечит: машины впритык без места для инсертера]\n7. Детали между машинами (печь → AM2 → AM2) передавай прямой вставкой. Обычный инсертер переносит ~0.83 предмета/с, поэтому на потоках больше этого ставь 2 инсертера параллельно. На одной ленте держи один тип предмета; разные ленты прокладывай по разные стороны ряда ассемблеров. [L3p1, L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput; лечит: заторы и узкие места]\n8. Закладывай запас 30% и больше: реальный выпуск ниже теоретического. Узкое место (одна печь, один инсертер) удваивай. [L3p1, L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput; лечит: недобор квоты]\n9. Выходной сундук заполняется быстро. Соедини через инсертеры 2–4 сундука. [L3p2:inserter_throughput, L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput; лечит: выпуск 0 на долгом прогоне]\n\nСтройка\n10. Ставь не дальше 10 тайлов от игрока. Переменная позиции игрока устаревает, поэтому в циклах вызывай move_to каждые несколько тайлов. Вдали от игрока can_place_entity возвращает False, так что для разведки он не годится. Лучше place_entity в try/except с проверкой через get_entity. [L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput; лечит: отказы стройки]\n11. place_entity может вернуть устаревший объект. Строй по явным координатам и перечитывай сущность через get_entity. Печатай pickup_position и drop_position инсертеров и при ошибке вызывай rotate_entity. [L3p1, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput; лечит: стройку не там и перевёрнутые инсертеры]\n12. Ленты ставь по одному тайлу с явным направлением; connect_entities лентами петляет. Перед длинной трассой проверь, нет ли на пути озера: get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, середина трассы). Обходи его вручную. [L3p1, L3p2:inserter_throughput, L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput; лечит: разрывы на воде]\n\nЭлектросеть\n13. connect_entities с MediumElectricPole иногда работает, но может оставить дыру или отдельную группу с voltage=0. После стройки проверь, что ElectricityGroup ровно одна, и найди сущности с NO_POWER или NOT_PLUGGED_IN, включая каждый двигатель. Покрытие столба ~3.5 тайла, провод тянется ~9 тайлов. [L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput, L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput, L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput; лечит: обесточенные машины]\n\nПроверки\n14. Первый замер завышен из-за буфера (53 против реальных 23). Перемерь через 60 с. [L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput; лечит: завышенную оценку]\n15. Burner-инсертер котла в статусе WAITING_FOR_SPACE с предупреждением «item on the ground» работает нормально. Суди о нём по уровню топлива в котле. [L3p2:iron_plate_throughput; лечит: ложную тревогу]\n16. Песочница запрещает getattr, import и двойные подчёркивания. Печатай только проблемные статусы, группы и топливо котла: get_entities() по всем лентам переполняет вывод. [L3p1, L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput; лечит: отклонённый код и потерю вывода]\n-----\n\nЭпизоды:\n[L1p1:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 74.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built an all-electric iron-plate factory. It used 14 of the 20 steps. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds a boiler at (2,4.5), which drives a steam engine at (14.5,8.5). The boiler's coal is mined automatically by two electric mining drills on the coal patch at (17.5,-1.5) and (17.5,1.5). They drop coal onto a straight belt I laid by hand: x=15.5 going down, then y=3.5 going left to x=4.5. A burner inserter at (3.5,3.5) moves the coal from the belt into the boiler. Iron: two electric mining drills on the iron patch at (19.5,73.5) and (25.5,73.5). Each drops ore straight into an electric furnace placed above it. An electric inserter takes the plates out into a wooden chest. Power re\nУроки головы: 1) Going all-electric (electric drills, electric furnaces, steam power) means only the boiler needs coal. Fuel logistics shrink to one coal belt plus one burner inserter. 2) An electric drill can drop ore straight into an electric furnace. Place the furnace with place_entity_next_to(drill.position, UP), then add an inserter on the far side and a chest at its drop_position. 3) connect_entities with belts over a long path that goes around obstacles produced a broken route with undergrounds and gaps. A short straight belt placed tile by tile with explicit directions worked. 4) Always check status after connect_entities for power poles. An inserter just outside a medium pole's coverage showed NO_POWER, and one extra pole fixed it. 5) A burner inserter tops up the boiler to only about 5-7 coal. That is normal: WAITING_FOR_SPACE_IN_DESTINATION with coal backed up on the belt means supply is enough. 6) get_entities with a set of belt prototypes once threw an error. Picking entities up by explicit position worked. 7) The throughput reported after each step (about 69) is higher than the theoretical 60 from two drills, so treat it only as a hint.\n\n[L1p1:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 37.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Built a fully electric gear factory that runs on its own coal. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds a boiler at (-5,4.5) and two steam engines at (0.5,8.5) and (5.5,8.5). Two electric mining drills on the coal patch at (19.5,5.5) and (19.5,9.5) put coal on a belt of about 22 tiles that ends at a burner inserter feeding the boiler. The burner inserter refuels itself from the coal it carries. As a backup that needs no electricity, a burner mining drill on coal at (16,3) drops onto the same belt, and a burner inserter picks coal off that belt to refuel the drill. This way power can restart even if the boiler runs dry and the electric drills stop. Production: two electric mining drills on\nУроки головы: 1) Electric furnaces and electric drills from the starting inventory remove almost all of the fuel logistics: only the boiler needs coal. 2) FLE inserter direction means the drop direction. Placed to the right of the boiler with direction=LEFT, the inserter feeds the boiler. Its status 'WAITING_FOR_SPACE / item on the ground' was wrong while it was in fact inserting. Check by watching the boiler's fuel count over time. 3) Inserters keep boiler fuel at only about 5 coal, so a manual stock of 50 drains down to that level. After a reset the boiler's buffer is only about 20 s at full load. 4) The electric loop 'electric coal drills, boiler' can deadlock. A burner mining drill on coal dropping onto the shared belt, refuelled by a burner inserter from that belt, makes the power restart without electricity. 5) Game time runs while each step's throughput is measured (60 s per step), so a mistake such as a wrongly turned inserter can empty the boiler between steps. 6) pickup_entity on one belt removes only that one tile, and connect_entities then does not re-lay the missing piece. The forbidden-code filter blocks getattr, and a step that fails with an error still counts.\n\n[L1p1:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.3/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Построил полностью электрический завод. Питание: offshore pump у воды (-9.5,1.5), бойлер (0,4.5), два паровых двигателя. Уголь добывают 2 электробура на угольном поле (17.5/20.5,-1.5), лента ведёт его к бойлеру, топливо закидывают 2 burner-инсертера. Бойлер держит 5–10 угля, это устойчивый режим. Медь: 2 электробура сбрасывают руду прямо в одну электропечь (-52.5,76.5). Дальше цепочка: инсертер → AM2 на медный провод → инсертер → AM2 на электросхемы → инсертер → деревянный сундук. Железо: 2 бура → электропечь (18.5,76.5) → инсертер → лента длиной 82 клетки → инсертер в сборщик схем. Электричество подвёл средними столбами, часть столбов пришлось ставить вручную. Печи электрические, поэтому вс\nУроки головы: 1) Электропечи из стартового инвентаря снимают проблему топлива печей: углём надо снабжать только бойлер. 2) Электробур может сбрасывать руду прямо в печь: два бура с разных сторон в одну печь работают без лент. 3) connect_entities для столбов иногда возвращает «успех», но сущность остаётся без питания (NO_POWER). Каждый раз проверяй status и добивай вручную через can_place_entity/place_entity; зона покрытия среднего столба 7x7, длина провода 9. 4) Инсертеры кладут в бойлер лишь небольшой запас топлива (около 5–10 штук), статус «WAITING_FOR_SPACE ... item on the ground» в этом случае вводит в заблуждение. Ручные 50 угля просто постепенно сгорают до этого уровня. 5) У инсертера direction — это направление выгрузки (LEFT: берёт справа, кладёт слева). 6) В коде запрещены getattr, __name__ и любые dunder; используй str(type(e)) и 'x' in dir(e). 7) Сущность, которую возвращает place_entity, иногда печатает чужую позицию; надёжнее перечитать через get_entity или get_entities.\n\n[L1p1:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic inserter factory, and the last throughput readings were 20 and 30 per minute against a quota of 16. The peak of 50 came from plates stored on the belts; the iron supply caps steady state at about 20–22 per minute, still above the quota.\n\n- **Power:** an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds one boiler at (2,4.5), which drives 2 steam engines (14.5,8.5 and 20.5,8.5), about 1.8 MW in total. Two electric drills on coal at x=17.5 drop onto a belt, and an electric inserter loads the boiler from it, so the boiler's fuel is fully automatic.\n- **Iron:** 3 electric drills (x=17.5/20.5/23.5, y=78.5), each dropping straight into an electric furnace above it. Inserters put the plat\nУроки головы: 1) place_entity / place_entity_next_to sometimes return a stale object (the coordinates of the previous entity). Check what was actually built with get_entities or get_entity before building connections on top of it.\n2) connect_entities for belts can produce staircase routes, silently fail to build anything when the target is an existing belt, and overwrite existing belts. Laying belts tile by tile with place_entity(TransportBelt, position, direction) is more reliable.\n3) can_place_entity does not catch water. A reliable probe is to place a wooden chest in try/except and pick it up again.\n4) An inserter's direction is the direction it drops into (direction=UP means it puts items above itself). This makes it easy to place inserters between assemblers directly.\n5) With 10 electric furnaces and electric drills in the inventory, a drill → electric furnace → inserter → belt chain needs no coal and no ore belts. The only thing that needs automated coal is the boiler (electric drill on coal → belt → inserter).\n6) 2 steam engines and 1 boiler (1.8 MW) are barely enough for 7 drills, 5 electric furnaces and 4 AM2 machines (LOW_POWER appears), so budget power ahead of time.\n7) getattr and similar built-ins are forbidden by the harness. BeltGroup has a .belts list, and each belt has .inventory, which is handy for diagnosing jams.\n\n[L1p1:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.0/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric automation-science-pack factory. It reached 21 packs/min against a quota of 16, and held that on every check from step 13 to 19. Power: an offshore pump feeds one boiler and two steam engines near (0,4). The boiler gets coal from two electric drills on the coal patch, carried by a long belt to a burner inserter. I added one burner mining drill on the same belt as a backup that runs without power, and topped the boiler up to 50 coal at the end so it can restart after the reset. Iron: two electric drills drop ore straight into two electric furnaces at (17,72); inserters put the plates on a belt into the assembly area. Copper: the same setup at (-48,72). Its belt goes a\nУроки головы: 1) place_entity with explicit coordinates and a direction is more predictable than connect_entities. For inserters the direction is the drop side (LEFT means it drops to the left). For belts it is the direction items travel. 2) connect_entities for belts can make strange long staircase routes (about 90 belts for 24 tiles), and around water it can quietly do nothing: it returned a single belt or connected nothing. Find water with get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, pos) and route by hand. 3) can_place_entity only works within the player's reach, so it cannot be used to scan the map from far away. 4) getattr and similar are forbidden. get_entity(e.prototype, ...) sometimes fails an assertion, so get_entities({Prototype.X}, position, radius) is more reliable. 5) When place_entity is called several times in a row, the returned object sometimes shows the previous position. Check the real layout with get_entities. 6) Rough capacity: electric drill straight into electric furnace gives about 30 plates/min; one assembling machine 2 makes 9 packs/min, so three cover a quota of 16 with margin. 7) Power is the weak point for the self-run: the burner inserter keeps only about 5 coal in the boiler, so after the reset the electric coal drills can lose power. A full boiler at the end and a burner drill on the coal belt guard against this. 8) Poles placed by hand in a grid, no more than 9 tiles apart, were more reliable than connect_entities with poles.\n\n[L1p1:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 22.2/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic logistic-science-pack factory. In the last steps the measured output was 17–18 packs/min against a quota of 16; the best reading was 18. Whether it holds through the 45-minute unattended run is not confirmed.\n\nWhat is built:\n- **Power plant 1:** an offshore pump, a boiler and 2 steam engines. Four electric drills on coal feed the boiler by belt and a burner inserter.\n- **Power plant 2:** a second offshore pump, a boiler and 2 steam engines that I hand-crafted mid-run. A coal drill drops into a chest, and a burner inserter moves coal from the chest into the boiler.\n- **Smelting:** iron uses 5 electric drills, each feeding an electric furnace directly, with output on \nУроки головы: 1) connect_entities with belts can take long, odd routes around water and other obstacles. Placing belts by hand, tile by tile with an explicit direction, is predictable and worked first time. 2) Plan the layout on paper first with fixed coordinates: tile occupancy, inserter direction (= the direction it drops) and pole coverage. A large build then goes up in a single step with no errors. 3) Power is the main bottleneck. Electric furnaces (180 kW), assembling machine 2s (150 kW) and electric drills (90 kW) quickly exceed 2 engines (1.8 MW). Plan for 4 or more engines from the start. You can hand-craft steam engines from gears in buffer chests plus iron plates pulled out of furnaces after temporarily removing their output inserters. 4) After connecting power, check every generator's ElectricityGroup and voltage. Poles placed by connect_entities can form a separate network with voltage=0 while the engine still reports WORKING. 5) Feed boilers as drill -> chest -> burner inserter -> boiler. The chest buffers coal and the burner inserter refuels itself, so the boiler keeps running even when power dips. 6) Put lane-separated items on one belt by having the two producers' inserters drop from opposite sides of the belt. This prevents one item flooding the belt and deadlocking the machines downstream. 7) The machine at the end of a belt can starve. Limit hungry consumers upstream (for example, use one input inserter on the gear machine). 8) The code filter rejects getattr, so print s\n\n[L1p2:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 37.3/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built an all-electric iron plate factory, and it measured 36 plates/min against a quota of 16. Power: an offshore pump at the lake (-9.5, 5.5) feeds a boiler at (16, 6.5) through a pipe about 25 tiles long. The boiler sits on the edge of the coal patch and drives one steam engine at (12.5, 6.5). An electric mining drill on coal at (18.5, 6.5) drops coal straight into the boiler. The boiler stayed full at 50 coal, so coal mining and fuel supply are fully automatic. A line of medium poles, laid by connect_entities, runs about 65 tiles south to the iron ore patch. There, two electric drills, at (20.5, 73.5) facing down and (20.5, 79.5) facing up, drop ore from both sides into one electric fur\nУроки головы: 1) A drill can drop coal straight into a boiler: place the drill on the edge of the coal patch, then the boiler with place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, LEFT, spacing=0). The drop point lands inside the boiler, and with no belts or inserters the fuel supply is fully automatic. 2) connect_entities(pump, boiler, Prototype.Pipe) built a working pipe of about 25 tiles over flat ground in one call. 3) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole ran a working 65-tile power line in one call. It does not cover every machine, though: a drill on the edge of a pole's 7x7 area got NO_POWER, and fixing it took one extra pole. Always check status after building. 4) A minimal block of 2 electric drills, 1 electric furnace, an inserter and a chest gives about 36 plates/min, so 16/min is easy. 5) Build in small steps with get_entities status checks after each one; it took only 6 steps. 6) place_entity_next_to returns the right coordinates for a boiler and steam engine, and their connection_points help with routing pipes.\n\n[L1p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 36.1/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric iron-gear-wheel factory in 6 steps. In my last steady-state measurements it made about 35 gears per minute, more than twice the quota of 16.\n\n- **Power:** an offshore pump at the water (-9.5, 1.5) is piped to a boiler at (10.5, 9), which feeds two steam engines connected in series.\n- **Boiler fuel:** two electric drills on the coal patch, at (17.5, 13.5) and (21.5, 13.5), drop coal onto a straight belt along y=11.5 that moves left. At its end a burner inserter at (10.5, 10.5) loads the boiler. The belt stays full and the boiler keeps about 5 coal topped up. At the end I added 45 coal to the boiler as a start-up reserve (it held 50 after the insert).\n- **Production:**\nУроки головы: 1. Each unit of 2 electric drills, 1 electric furnace and 1 assembling machine 2 made about 17-18 gears per minute, because the furnace (about 37 plates per minute) is the bottleneck. Building two units gave a 2x margin.\n2. A boiler placed facing UP takes water on its short ends and outputs steam upward. That leaves the bottom long side free for the burner inserter and the coal belt.\n3. place_entity_next_to(SteamEngine, eng.position, UP, spacing=0) chained a second engine onto the first with no extra pipe. It reported NOT_CONNECTED at first but showed WORKING by the next step, after I had also added a pole next to it.\n4. connect_entities with MediumElectricPole over about 60 tiles worked on the first try and gave a single network with voltage above 0.\n5. The drop_position returned for the second drill in a loop was stale (the coordinates of an earlier drill). The drill itself was placed correctly, so check by re-reading entities and their status, not the returned object.\n6. Hand-placing belts tile by tile in a straight line, with the drills facing the belt, worked straight away for feeding the boiler.\n7. Planning in one or two large steps with fixed coordinates got the whole factory built in 6 steps.\n\n[L1p2:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Built a fully electric electronic-circuit factory in 10 of 20 steps. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) pipes water to a boiler at (15,0.5) on the coal patch, which feeds two steam engines. An electric mining drill at (17.5,0.5) drops coal straight into the boiler, so the boiler stays at 50 coal and needs no belts or inserters. Iron: 2 electric drills feed an electric furnace at (17.5,72.5). An inserter puts plates on a 73-tile belt that runs west to the copper site. The belt had to go around a lake at x -21..-9, y>=69, so part of it runs along y=68.5. Copper: 2 drills feed an electric furnace at (-50.5,72.5). From there it is direct insertion: inserter -> cable AM2 -> inserter -> circuit\nУроки головы: 1. An electric drill can drop coal straight into the boiler's fuel slot (place the drill, then place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, side)). This keeps power running by itself, with no belts or inserters. Check that drill.drop_position falls inside the boiler's area. 2. An electric furnace is 3x3, not 2x2. Building a straight column with place_entity_next_to (drill UP -> furnace -> inserter -> AM2 -> inserter -> AM2 -> inserter -> chest) gives clean, predictable coordinates. 3. A second drill beside the furnace (place_entity_next_to LEFT/RIGHT, then rotate it toward the furnace) brings the furnace to its 37.5 plates/min. 4. A long connect_entities run with medium poles detoured around water and built a separate grid with voltage 0. Placing poles by hand every 8 tiles along a free row was reliable. 5. When laying belts tile by tile, collect the failures from place_entity. Find the water with get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, pos), then detour by hand with corners (UP -> LEFT -> DOWN) and pick up the old orphaned tiles. 6. can_place_entity also marks tiles taken by your own belts and only works within the player's reach. Read its probe map with care. 7. Check where a burner drill actually drops: a 2x2 burner drill next to a boiler that also has a drill beside it can end up dropping into the wrong entity.\n\n[L1p2:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 33.9/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric inserter factory in 9 of the 20 steps. It runs at about 30 inserters/min at steady state against a quota of 16.\n\n- **Power:** an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5), a boiler at (-5,4.5) and 2 steam engines. Two electric drills on coal at (17.5,2.5) and (17.5,6.5) drop onto one belt cell from opposite sides. The 22-tile belt along y=4.5 feeds a self-fuelling burner inserter at (-3.5,4.5) that loads the boiler.\n- **Iron:** 4 electric furnaces in a row at y=74.5, each fed by a drill below it (facing UP). Output inserters put plates on a belt (y=71.5, then x=14.5, then y=64.5) that runs under the assemblers.\n- **Copper:** 2 furnaces with one drill each at x=-48.5 and -52.5. The\nУроки головы: 1. can_place_entity and nearest do not reveal a lake in the middle of a route. Before laying a long belt, check get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, pos).bounding_box near the route, or wrap each placement in try/except and print the failures so you can reroute in the next step.\n2. Bypassing an obstacle is easy by side-loading: lay a parallel belt and run it into the side of the existing perpendicular belt.\n3. Linking AMs directly with inserters (cable->circuit->inserter<-gear) needs no intermediate belts. A basic inserter moves about 50 items/min, so put 2 inserters on the cable->circuit link.\n4. A put(proto,x,y,dir) helper with move_to and try/except, plus manual pole and belt grids, let me build the whole factory in one step without errors. Variables and functions persist between steps.\n5. The burner inserter keeps only about 5-6 coal in the boiler, so a manual top-up drains back down within a minute. Top up the boiler to 50 on the very last step.\n6. With 2 steam engines (1.8 MW) and 8 drills, 6 furnaces and 4 AM2s, LOW_POWER appears, but output still holds at about 30/min because production is planned with a margin. Estimate the power budget against the inventory beforehand: there may be no spare engines.\n7. The coal drills, belt and burner inserter to the boiler keep power running on their own. Two electric drills (60/min) cover one boiler (27/min at full load) with a margin.\n\n[L1p2:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 35.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric, self-supplying automation-science-pack factory. The best measured throughput was 31 packs per 60 s, against a quota of 16.\n\n- **Power:** an offshore pump feeds a boiler at (0,2.5), which drives 2 steam engines at (12.5,6.5) and (17.5,6.5). Two electric drills on the coal patch at (17.5,-2.5) and (17.5,1.5) drop onto one 18-tile belt along y=-0.5. A burner inserter at (0.5,0.5) takes coal off that belt into the boiler. I filled the boiler to 49 coal at the end. The boiler burns about 20 coal/min and the drills supply about 60/min, and boiler fuel stayed stable.\n- **Iron:** 2 electric drills feed 2 electric furnaces directly (drill outputs UP). Inserters put the plate\nУроки головы: 1) Don't reuse global loop variable names (x) across loops in one step. Iron furnaces and inserters inside a for-loop came out at x=0.5 instead of 17.5/21.5. Give each loop its own variable, or place critical items with literal coordinates, and always list entities with their positions after building.\n2) A helper that calls move_to plus place_entity with fixed coordinates, laying belts tile by tile, built a whole 6-AM2 factory in one step with no errors.\n3) Direct insertion works well. Gear AM2 sits between two sci AM2s with inserters in the gaps, so no gear belt is needed. Use separate iron and copper belts on either side of the assembler row.\n4) For the boiler fuel feed: burner inserter on the side of the boiler free of pipes, coal belt from electric coal drills. Before finishing, top the boiler up to about 50 coal to survive the reset, when the belts are emptied.\n5) With 2 steam engines, a load of 6 AM2 + 3 electric furnaces + 5 drills had no power issues, because real load is below nameplate.\n6) Medium poles placed by hand in the gaps between machines join automatically into one ElectricityGroup. Check NO_POWER via the statuses from get_entities.\n\n[L1p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.8/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric logistic-science-pack factory that steadily makes 23–25 packs per minute against a quota of 16. The 45-minute run after the reset could not be checked; that figure comes from the per-step measurements, which are only a hint.\n\n- **Power:** 2 offshore pumps, 2 boilers and 4 steam engines (3.6 MW). The task inventory had only 2 steam engines. I built 2 more by hand from iron plates taken out of my own furnaces plus pipes already in the inventory.\n- **Coal:** 3 electric drills on the coal patch feed a belt. Two burner inserters take coal from the end of that belt into the boilers. Boiler coal held steady at 4–7 units over 60 seconds, and I topped both boilers up to 50 at\nУроки головы: 1. Count power at full load before building. With 5 furnaces, 13 drills and 9 AM2s, 1.8 MW gave LOW_POWER everywhere. If the inventory is short of steam engines, take iron plates from your own furnaces and hand-craft them with craft_item (engine: 8 gears, 10 plates, 5 pipes).\n2. Lakes can sit right on the route and nearest() won't show them. Before laying a long belt, call get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, point_on_route) and look at the bounding_box. Placing a belt on water gives a clear error, so collect the errors and reroute the belt.\n3. Use one helper P(proto,x,y,dir) that calls move_to when needed and puts exceptions in a list. Then a large block (around 100 entities) builds in a single step and you see every failure.\n4. Placing a series of objects with place_entity can drift: two inserters and chests ended up at x=32.5 instead of 22.5. After a large build, list the entities with get_entities and fix any strays.\n5. To put two products on one belt without blocking each other, give each its own lane. One item goes on by an inserter (it drops onto the far lane). The other comes in by side-loading from a short belt on the same side (it lands on the near lane).\n6. The burner inserter keeps only about 5 coal in the boiler. A full boiler burns down to that level, which is normal. Judge supply by whether that level holds steady over time.\n7. Two boilers can be fed from the last tile of one coal belt, with burner inserters on opposite sides of that tile.\n\n[L2p1:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 74.4/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric iron-plate factory that runs itself, in 9 steps. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,12.5) is piped to a boiler at (20.5,7) on the coal patch, and the boiler feeds a steam engine at (20.5,2.5). An electric mining drill at (20.5,9.5) mines coal and drops it straight into the boiler, so the boiler refuels itself. Only the first 20 coal were added by hand. Production: a line of medium electric poles runs from y=3 to y=73 to the iron patch. There are two identical lines at x=18.5 and x=24.5. Each has an electric mining drill (y=75.5) that drops ore straight into an electric furnace (y=72.5). An electric inserter moves plates from the furnace into a wooden chest (y=69.5). Fu\nУроки головы: 1) The simplest closed fuel loop: an electric mining drill on coal dropping straight into a boiler. Its drop_position lands inside the boiler, so no belts or inserters are needed. 2) Electric furnaces need no fuel, which removes all coal logistics for smelting; an electric drill can drop ore straight into a furnace. 3) connect_entities(pole, entity, MediumElectricPole) may stop one pole short of the target. Check status (NO_POWER) and add a pole by hand next to the entity. A medium pole covers about ±3.5 tiles. 4) A one-tile gap between the boiler's steam output and the steam engine has to be bridged with connect_entities(boiler, engine, Pipe). 5) The sandbox rejects getattr/import, and get_entity(e.prototype, ...) can fail with AssertionError. To check status, use get_entities(position=..., radius=...) instead. 6) place_entity_next_to(Inserter, furnace, UP) gave an inserter that already takes from the furnace (pickup next to the furnace), so no rotation was needed. Check pickup_position anyway.\n\n[L2p1:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 36.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic, all-electric gear factory. It produced 35-36 gears per minute against a quota of 16, about 2.2x.\n\nPower: an offshore pump at (-9.5, 1.5) feeds a boiler at (-5, 4.5), which drives a steam engine at (7.5, 8.5). Fuel is automatic. An electric mining drill on the coal patch at (17.5, 2.5) drops coal onto a 21-belt line. An electric inserter at (-3.5, 4.5) loads the boiler from that belt. Over two minutes the boiler's fuel dropped to 5 coal and then refilled to 8, so the coal loop keeps it supplied.\n\nPower reaches the iron patch over a line of medium electric poles running about 70 tiles south.\n\nIron and gears: there are two electric furnaces, at (25.5, 80.5) and (29.5,\nУроки головы: 1) The starting inventory includes electric drills, electric furnaces, assembling machine 2 and electric inserters. An all-electric build with one coal-fed boiler is the simplest way to make everything automatic.\n2) An electric mining drill drops ore straight into an electric furnace if it is placed next to the furnace facing it. Two drills on two sides can feed one furnace, so no belts are needed.\n3) place_entity with exact coordinates and a direction works reliably. An inserter's direction is the side it drops onto. Check pickup_position and drop_position after placing.\n4) connect_entities with medium poles sometimes stops short of the target. Look for the not-plugged-in status and add a bridging pole by hand (wire reach is about 9 tiles). A pole powers about 3.5 tiles around itself, so place poles right next to inserters.\n5) A fuel inserter that shows WAITING_FOR_SPACE / 'blocked' is normal: it only tops the boiler up to a few coal. Check over time that the boiler's fuel does not fall to zero.\n6) The sandbox rejects getattr and import. Print entity objects directly.\n7) A wooden chest holds 1600 gears. A second inserter-and-chest buffer is cheap insurance against the output backing up.\n\n[L2p1:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 25.0/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic, all-electric electronic-circuit factory. It held a steady 23 circuits/min against a quota of 16.\n\nPower: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds a boiler at (2,4.5), which drives two steam engines at (14.5,8.5) and (23.5,16.5). Two electric drills on the coal patch at (19.5,3.5) and (19.5,6.5) send coal along an 18-belt line to an electric inserter that fuels the boiler. The drills supply about 60 coal/min and the boiler burns about 20/min. The belt stays backed up and the boiler holds 4–5 coal.\n\nIron: one electric drill at (17.5,79.5) drops ore straight into an electric furnace. An inserter puts the plates on a belt to the assembly area.\n\nCopper: two drills drop ore \nУроки головы: 1) Electric furnaces plus electric drills avoid most fuel automation: only the boiler needs coal. That supply is two coal drills, a belt and an inserter into the boiler.\n2) A drill can drop ore straight into an electric furnace placed at its drop position, and two drills facing each other can feed one furnace. Then furnace, inserter, belt.\n3) The interpreter does not handle tuple assignment properly (X, Y = a, b kept the old values). Assign each variable separately. getattr and similar are banned.\n4) Check placement with nearest_buildable: fixed coordinates can land on water and waste a step.\n5) For inserters, direction is the drop direction. Check pickup_position and drop_position after placing.\n6) Count power demand. One steam engine (900 kW) is not enough for 5 drills, 2 furnaces and 2 assembling-machine-2. A second engine joined by connect_entities(eng, eng2, Pipe) works, but its pole can end up in a separate network with zero voltage. Add a linking pole.\n7) A medium pole can block a belt run, and connect_entities with a belt does not reliably join a second drill to an existing belt. Placing the belts by hand is more dependable.\n8) Check status and warnings on every entity. 'WAITING_FOR_SPACE' on a supply belt that is backed up is normal.\n\n[L2p1:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 28.1/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic, electric inserter factory. Over the last 60 s check it made 25 inserters per minute, against a quota of 16.\n\nPower: an offshore pump, 1 boiler and 2 steam engines. Two electric drills on the coal patch put coal on a belt. A burner inserter feeds the boiler from that belt and refuels itself from the coal it carries.\n\nIron: 3 electric drills, each dropping ore straight into an electric furnace, about 90 plates/min. Inserters put the plates on a belt that runs west along y=67.5.\n\nCopper: 2 more drill and furnace pairs on the copper patch, about 60 plates/min, on a 53-tile belt running east.\n\nAssembly: a row of four assembling-machine-2 at y=64.5. Left to right they ma\nУроки головы: 1) place_entity sometimes returns the wrong entity, often an earlier one of the same type. get_entity can return None instead of raising an error. So always look entities up again with get_entity/get_entities at the exact position and check for None. Don't rely on try/except.\n2) An inserter's direction is the side it drops on (UP drops north). Print pickup_position and drop_position to confirm.\n3) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole leaves gaps in coverage. Afterwards check every entity for NO_POWER and place extra poles by hand on free tiles (supply area 7x7, wire reach 9).\n4) Placing an electric drill so it drops directly into an electric furnace (furnace 3 tiles above the drill, drill facing UP) is a compact way to get about 30 plates/min per pair with no ore belts.\n5) One boiler with 2 engines (1.8 MW) is enough for about 6 drills, 5 furnaces and 4 AM2s. Coal from 2 electric drills and a belt to a burner inserter keeps the boiler fuelled with no manual coal.\n6) The harness bans getattr and import, and get_entities takes no prototype argument. Filter by e.name.\n7) The first throughput reading is inflated by stockpiled parts. Measure steady state by counting the chest contents before and after sleep(60).\n\n[L2p1:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.4/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric automation-science-pack factory. The last measured throughput was 24 packs per minute against a quota of 16. Power comes from an offshore pump, 1 boiler and 2 steam engines. The boiler is fed by a burner inserter from a belt carrying coal from 2 electric mining drills on the coal patch at (17,2–5), so the coal supply needs no manual input. Iron: 2 electric drills at (17.5/20.5, 72.5) drop straight into electric furnaces, which need no fuel. Inserters move the plates onto a belt that runs north and then west along y=59.5. Copper: 1 drill and 1 electric furnace at (-48.5, 70), with a belt running east along y=65.5. Assembly: two gear assemblers (AM2) each take iron fro\nУроки головы: 1) If the inventory has electric furnaces and electric drills, use them. Then the only fuel to automate is coal for the boiler: a burner inserter fed by a coal belt from the drills. 2) An electric drill facing UP with an electric furnace placed exactly 3 tiles north (place_entity with explicit coordinates) feeds the furnace with no inserter. place_entity and place_entity_next_to sometimes return a neighbouring entity by mistake, so check the result with get_entities. 3) An inserter's direction is the direction it drops items. Placing it with an explicit direction= is simpler than rotating it afterwards. 4) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole often leaves entities on the edge of a pole's coverage unpowered (NO_POWER). Check statuses and place extra poles by hand. Before building, check that no trunk pole stands where you plan to build. 5) Assembler-to-assembler insertion (gears to a pack assembler on each side) avoids mixed belts and lane deadlocks. Iron and copper on separate belts, coming in from opposite sides of the row, works reliably. 6) 2 AM2 pack assemblers give 18/min in theory but measured only 16. Build about 50% above quota. 7) Avoid getattr and similar constructs: the harness filter rejects them. Print the entities themselves or their attributes directly.\n\n[L2p1:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 22.8/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic, all-electric logistic science pack factory. The last three checks showed 20, 19 and 19 packs per 60 s against a quota of 16. Every entity was powered and the ore and coal lines were backed up with surplus. I did not simulate the 45-minute unattended run, so the 45-minute self-sufficiency is reasoned from design, not measured.\n\n- **Power:** 2 boilers and 4 steam engines, about 3.6 MW, with 2 offshore pumps. Boiler 1 gets coal from 2 electric drills by belt and 2 burner inserters. Boiler 2 is fed directly by an electric drill dropping into it.\n- **Iron:** 5 electric drills each drop straight into an electric furnace (about 150 plates/min against about 88 needed). Two\nУроки головы: 1) place_entity sometimes returns the wrong object (a nearby one of the same type), so always re-read the entity with get_entity(proto, pos) after placing it.\n2) A connect_entities belt call whose start equals its end fails ('Invalid path length'). A route that turns at an existing belt end is more reliable when you lay the belts by hand with place_entity and an explicit direction.\n3) Check power right away: one steam engine stayed unplugged without any error, and a power shortage combined with a coal belt that was never built caused a blackout. Electric drills feeding the coal can spiral down under low power, so leave a power margin. You can hand-craft extra steam engines from hand-mined ore smelted in temporary stone furnaces.\n4) An electric drill dropping straight into an electric furnace or a boiler is the simplest automatic ore and fuel chain. Burner inserters on a coal belt refuel themselves.\n5) For two products on one belt, place their output inserters on opposite sides so each product gets its own lane and the belt cannot deadlock.\n6) Check the map for water before laying out (get_resource_patch for Water). A second lake blocked one of my assembler spots.\n7) Inserter direction means the drop direction (RIGHT means it picks from the west and drops to the east), and a drill's direction sets where it drops.\n8) A boiler fed by inserters only holds about 5–7 coal; that is the inserter fill limit, not a shortage.\n\n[L2p2:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 73.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Built a fully electric iron-plate factory with no manual inputs, in 12 steps. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,4.5) sends water by pipe to a boiler at (14.5,5), which sits on the edge of the coal patch. An electric mining drill at (17.5,4.5), facing LEFT, drops coal straight into the boiler. Two steam engines stand north of the boiler, joined to it by pipes. The boiler stayed full at 50 coal; the coal drill showed WAITING_FOR_SPACE, which means it keeps up. Medium electric poles (laid with connect_entities, plus 4 extra poles placed by hand) carry power about 75 tiles to the iron patch. Production: two columns at x=18.5 and x=26.5. Each column has an electric furnace at y=77.5 with two elect\nУроки головы: 1) A boiler can sit on the coal patch edge with an electric drill dropping into it: place the drill first, then the boiler centred at drill.drop_position minus 1 tile, with water piped in from the pump 25 tiles away. connect_entities(pump, boiler, Pipe) worked first try. 2) In an electric drill, furnace, drill sandwich (drills 3 tiles either side facing the furnace), drop_position lands exactly in the furnace. One such column gives about 36 plates/min. 3) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole over 75 tiles built the line, but it left one column and an inserter without power. Check NO_POWER after a sleep and add poles by hand next to the buildings. 4) place_entity has a range of about 10 tiles, so call move_to near the target before each group of placements. 5) get_entities() also returns PipeGroup and ElectricityGroup objects, which have no .warnings attribute; filter them out by name. 6) Measure output as the change in chest contents over sleep(60), and check that boiler fuel holds steady, rather than trusting the first status reading.\n\n[L2p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 56.2/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Построил полностью электрический автоматический завод шестерёнок за 9 шагов. Энергия: насос на воде у (-9.5,3.5), трубы ведут к котлу (14.5,9) у края угольного поля. Электробур (17.5,8.5) смотрит LEFT и сбрасывает уголь прямо в котёл, котёл стабильно держит 50 угля. Над котлом стоят два паровых двигателя в линию (центры y=5.5 и 0.5, direction UP), между ними нет труб. Столбы до железного поля (~75 клеток) проложены через connect_entities(MediumElectricPole). Производство: AM2 с рецептом шестерёнок в (27.5,80.5). С запада, севера и востока стоят цепочки «электробур → электропечь в точке drop_position → inserter в AM2». На выходе два inserter'а и два деревянных сундука. Первый замер показал 85\nУроки головы: 1) Схема «электробур → электропечь в drop_position → inserter → AM2» работает сразу. Три такие цепочки с трёх сторон AM2 дают около 53 шестерёнок/мин. Печь ставить на drop_position + 1 клетку по направлению бура. 2) Котёл ставить прямо на точку сброса угольного бура: 3 клетки от центра бура, котёл direction UP. Бур закрывает одну водяную точку подключения, вода идёт через вторую, и котёл сам заполняется до 50 угля. 3) Двигатели direction UP можно ставить вплотную над steam_output_point котла и друг над другом (шаг 5 клеток): пар доходит без труб. 4) connect_entities(pos, pos, MediumElectricPole) на 75 клеток сработал. Сущности на краю зоны (выходные манипуляторы) остались без питания, их нашёл по NO_POWER и поставил ещё один столб. 5) place_entity ограничен дистанцией 10 от игрока: перед каждой группой построек делать move_to. 6) В get_entities() попадает PipeGroup без поля warnings. Фильтровать через 'Group' in str(type(e)) нужно до обращения к атрибутам, иначе цикл падает. 7) Первый замер после запуска завышен (85 против 53) из-за запаса пластин. Мерить несколько минут подряд.\n\n[L2p2:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.7/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric electronic-circuit factory, and the last measurement showed 23 circuits per minute against a quota of 16. I measured this myself in steady state: the output chest went from 83 to 106 over 60 seconds. The harness readings were 23 and 22.\n\nPower: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds a boiler at (14.5,5) through a pipe about 25 tiles long. Two steam engines sit right next to the boiler on its steam output, with no pipe between them. An electric mining drill on coal drops coal straight into the boiler, which kept 50 coal the whole time.\n\nIron: one electric drill at (18.5,78.5) drops ore into an electric furnace at (15.5,78.5). An inserter puts plates on a 32-tile belt ru\nУроки головы: 1) An electric furnace is 3x3, not 2x2. Place it 3 tiles out from the drill centre: the drill at x=18.5 facing west drops at 16.5, and the furnace centre goes at 15.5. Placing it exactly on drop_position collides with the drill.\n2) Ore patches can have lakes in between. Run get_resource_patch(Water) on the assembly area before building, and put the assembly row next to the lake rather than routing belts around it.\n3) Put the boiler right on a coal patch, fed by a drill whose drop point is inside the boiler. Bring water with connect_entities(pump, boiler, Pipe); 25 tiles works. A steam engine placed with direction UP directly on the boiler's steam_output_point connects with no pipes at all.\n4) One cable AM2 and one circuit AM2 easily cover about 25 circuits per minute. Cable moves between the assemblers at 1.25 per second, so use three inserters on the shared edge, because one basic inserter manages about 0.83 items per second. Smelting is the real limit: one electric furnace gives about 37 plates per minute, even with two drills feeding it.\n5) In placement loops, call move_to before each section, because the character can only reach 10 tiles. A shared counter across loops caused a \"too far\" error.\n6) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole lays long, winding lines and leaves end buildings unpowered (here the output inserter and the copper drills). Check for NO_POWER and add poles by hand.\n7) Do not use getattr, even inside a condition: the whole step is rejected. get_entitie\n\n[L2p2:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric inserter factory. Measured steady output is 23 inserters/min against a quota of 16. Power comes from an offshore pump at water (-9.5,0.5) and about 25 tiles of pipe to a boiler placed next to the coal patch. An electric drill on coal drops straight into the boiler, which stays topped up at 50 coal, so fuel is fully automatic. The boiler drives 2 steam engines (1.8 MW), and a line of medium poles runs about 70 tiles south to the ore patches. Iron: 3 drills facing UP drop into 3 electric furnaces, and a 4th drill feeds one furnace from the side. Inserters move the plates onto a belt to the factory. Copper: 2 drills feed 1 electric furnace, and a 56-tile belt goes aroun\nУроки головы: 1) Water bodies can sit directly in the path between patches: get_resource_patch(Water, ..., radius=20) on the route before laying belts or poles; I hit a lake at x -22..-9.5, y 69..92 and lost a step. 2) Instead of a coal belt, pipe water from the pump to a boiler at the coal patch edge: place the electric drill first (direction=LEFT), then place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, LEFT) — the drop lands in the boiler and it holds 50 coal on its own. 3) place_entity really does return a neighbouring entity of the same type in printouts, but the entity itself gets placed correctly — check with get_entities, not the return value. 4) place_entity has a range limit of 10 tiles: call move_to right next to the target before every placement in loops. 5) The second steam engine is often left without a pole (NOT_PLUGGED_IN): add a pole by hand next to it, otherwise everything sits at LOW_POWER. 6) can_place_entity far from the player returns False everywhere, so it is useless as a water map. 7) A chain of 4 AM2 machines with direct inserter handoff (2 inserters for cable) plus 1 copper furnace fed by 2 drills gives about 23 inserters/min; the bottleneck is copper. 8) Wooden-chest delta over sleep(60) matched the harness figure (23 vs 22).\n\n[L2p2:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Built a fully electric automation-science-pack factory. Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) pipes water to a boiler at (22.5,4) on the coal patch. Two electric drills drop coal straight into the boiler (from the south and the east). Two steam engines are connected directly to the boiler, giving 1.8 MW. Iron (y≈69.5): 2 electric drills drop ore into 2 electric furnaces. Each furnace feeds an AM2 making gears through an inserter. The gear inserter puts gears on the north lane of a belt running east along y=66.5. Copper (x≈-49.5): a drill feeds an electric furnace. An inserter puts the plates on a belt that goes north and turns east, so copper rides the south lane of the same belt for about 8\nУроки головы: 1) Check the gap between an assembler or furnace and its inserter: a 3x3 at y=62.5 covers 61..64, so an inserter at 65.5 drops at 64.5, onto the ground. Center the building so drop_position falls inside it (furnace/AM at y=Ybelt-3 when the inserter is at Ybelt-1). 2) An electric drill drops coal into a boiler only if drop_position is inside the boiler's tiles: the boiler at y=4 spans 3..5, so the drill goes at y=6.5, not 7.5. Two coal drills from different sides keep the boiler at 50 coal. 3) Lane trick: copper is inserted from the west onto a north-going belt, so after the right turn east it sits on the south lane; gears inserted from the south of the eastbound belt go on the north lane. Mixing on one belt causes no deadlock. 4) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole over ~70 tiles left the far end unpowered. A manual chain of poles every 7 tiles fixed it at once. get_entities returns ElectricityGroup/BeltGroup/PipeGroup objects, which have no warnings, voltage or position fields, so filter by type before reading attributes. 5) Any exception aborts the rest of the step, so wrap risky placements in try/except. Keep within 10 tiles: call move_to before each placement, including at the start of a loop. 6) Three AM2s on automation-science-pack (27/min theoretical) with 2 iron and 1 copper drill+furnace pairs gave a steady 24/min on one boiler and 2 engines without blackouts.\n\n[L2p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.8/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric logistic science pack factory. In the last steps it made 21–24 packs/min against a quota of 16. That is a lower bound from the 60-second checks: the 45-minute run with emptied buffers was not tested directly.\n\nPower: 2 boilers and 4 steam engines (3.6 MW), with 2 offshore pumps. Each boiler gets coal from an electric drill that drops straight into it. Boiler 1 also has a backup drill feeding it through a chest and an inserter. The last two steam engines were hand-crafted from 60 iron ore I mined by hand and smelted in temporary furnaces, which I then removed.\n\nRaw materials: 4 iron units, each an electric furnace fed by 2 drills, at roughly 30–37 plates/min per unit.\nУроки головы: 1. Count the starting inventory first. With only 1 boiler and 2 engines (1.8 MW), a 10-AM2 factory with 9 drills and 5 furnaces is short of power and holds at about 16/min. You can hand-craft extra steam engines with craft_item: mine about 60 iron ore by hand, smelt it in temporary electric furnaces, then extract the plates.\n2. A water bounding box from get_resource_patch can sit right between two ore patches. Check for water with get_resource_patch(Water, centre, radius) and nearest(Water) after move_to, before laying a long belt. can_place_entity with an item not in the inventory returns False everywhere and wastes a step.\n3. An inserter feeding a 3x3 machine must stand on the tile next to its edge. For a machine centred at y, that is y+2 picking from y+3, not y+3 picking from y+4. Check that drop_position is inside the machine's footprint.\n4. Keep two products on separate belts (P1 for inserters, P2 for transport belts) with the science row between them. This avoids a mixed-lane deadlock without lane tricks.\n5. connect_entities(boiler, engine, Pipe) can attach to the boiler's spare water inlet and join the engine to the water line. A pipe next to another pipe always merges with it. Lay steam pipes by hand from steam_output_point, at least one tile away from water pipes. A pipe that held water must be picked up and placed again.\n6. A boiler showing 'chest is full' with 50 coal means it is fully fuelled. The drill or inserter warning 'output blocked by item on the ground' th\n\n[L3p1:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 75.0/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric iron-plate factory that needs no hand-fed fuel. It ran at 69–70 iron plates per 60 s against a quota of 16. Power comes from an offshore pump at water (-9.5,1.5), a boiler at (0,4.5) and a steam engine at (12.5,8.5). The boiler's coal is automated: an electric mining drill on the coal patch at (19.5,5.5) drops coal onto a 17-tile belt, and a burner inserter at (1.5,4.5) loads it into the boiler. That inserter refuels itself from the coal it carries. Medium electric poles run about 65 tiles south to the iron patch. There are two identical lines, with drills at (19.5,72.5) and (25.5,72.5). In each line an electric mining drill faces UP and drops ore straight into an el\nУроки головы: 1) Avoid burner chains: an inserter that takes plates out of a furnace cannot refuel itself, so use power (pump, boiler, steam engine) with electric drills, furnaces and inserters. Then the only fuel needed is coal into the boiler, delivered by a burner inserter that refuels itself from the coal it carries. 2) An electric drill can drop ore straight into an electric furnace placed with place_entity_next_to(drill.position, UP), and an electric inserter on the far side moves plates to a chest. 3) Running connect_entities with MediumElectricPole across several entities left gaps (some machines got NO_POWER). After connecting, check every entity's status and fill gaps by placing poles by hand (supply area about ±3.5 tiles). 4) After place_entity_next_to, an inserter takes FROM the reference entity, so rotate it when it should feed into that entity instead. 5) The code filter rejects getattr and import, so use print(entity) and get_entities() for diagnostics. 6) The doc's patterns (nearest_buildable plus a BuildingBox for the boiler and steam engine, connect_entities with Pipe) worked on the first try.\n\n[L3p1:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 37.6/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built an all-electric iron-gear-wheel factory that runs on its own. Power: an offshore pump at the water (-9.5,1.5) feeds a boiler at (3,0.5), which feeds a steam engine at (3.5,10.5). The boiler gets its coal automatically: an electric mining drill on the coal patch at (17.5,-1.5) drops coal onto a belt, and an electric inserter at (3.5,-1.5) loads it into the boiler. A line of medium electric poles runs about 70 tiles south to the iron patch. Production at the iron patch is centred on an assembling-machine-2 at (27.5,83.5) set to gears. On each side, an electric mining drill drops ore straight into an electric furnace (west at 20.5/23.5, east at 34.5/31.5). An inserter moves the plates f\nУроки головы: 1) The game kit includes electric drills, electric furnaces and assembling-machine-2, so the only thing that needs fuel is the boiler, which makes automating fuel much simpler. 2) An inserter's direction is the side it drops on: DOWN takes from above and drops below. Check pickup_position and drop_position after placing. 3) An electric drill can drop ore straight into a furnace placed at its drop_position, with no belts or chests. 4) A boiler inserter showing WAITING_FOR_SPACE_IN_DESTINATION with an 'item on the ground' warning is not a fault: inserters only top up fuel to a limit of about 5–8 coal. Judge it by the boiler's fuel level over time. 5) A medium pole has to actually cover the entity. connect_entities from one entity to another sometimes fails ('nil value'), and placing poles by hand next to the drills fixes it. 6) getattr and similar built-ins are forbidden. Print the whole entity to see its fields. 7) pickup_entity on a belt picks up only one tile, not the whole belt group.\n\n[L3p1:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 37.0/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic electronic-circuit factory with no manual inputs. It ran at about 40 circuits per minute in steady state, against a quota of 16. The best reading I saw was 47, but that one included buffered stock.\n\n- **Power:** one offshore pump feeds one boiler, which drives two steam engines. The second engine is piped off the existing steam line.\n- **Boiler fuel:** two electric mining drills on the coal patch put coal on a belt. A burner inserter loads it into the boiler, and it refuels itself from the coal it carries.\n- **Iron:** one module of two electric drills dropping ore straight into an electric furnace from both sides. An inserter takes plates from the furnace onto a bel\nУроки головы: 1) Check the starting inventory first. Here it had electric furnaces, electric drills and assembling machine 2, so I could make everything electric and only the boiler needs fuel. That removes most fuel logistics.\n2) An electric drill can drop ore straight into an electric furnace. Placing two drills facing each other with the furnace between them works well and needs no belts on the mining side.\n3) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole does not always reach small entities like inserters. Check for NO_POWER status and place a pole next to them by hand.\n4) The sandbox rejects getattr and any code containing double underscores, as well as import. Use plain attribute access such as e.status and e.warnings.\n5) connect_entities with pipes fails if the engine's connection point is blocked, here by a belt. Starting a new pipe next to an existing steam pipe and running it to the new engine works.\n6) Inserter rotation is easiest to get right by checking drop_position after placing and calling rotate_entity only if it points the wrong way.\n7) A single electric furnace (37.5 plates per minute) limits copper to about 25 circuits per minute. Adding parallel inserters between the cable and circuit machines is a cheap way to avoid an inserter limit on cable transfer.\n8) The first throughput reading includes buffered stock. Wait 30 to 60 seconds and read again to see the real steady rate.\n\n[L3p1:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 29.2/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: Built a fully electric inserter factory. Power: an offshore pump feeds 1 boiler, which feeds 2 steam engines. The boiler gets coal automatically from 4 electric drills on the coal patch over two belts, through an electric inserter and a self-fuelling burner inserter. Smelting: 3 electric drills on iron and 2 on copper each drop ore straight into an electric furnace, and an inserter puts the plates on a belt. Assembly (4 assembling-machine-2): copper cable feeds circuits through 2 inserters, circuits and gears are inserted directly into the inserter assembler, and iron comes off a belt into the circuit, gear and inserter assemblers. Output goes into a chest, plus a second chest after another \nУроки головы: 1) place_entity sometimes returns a stale object for a neighbouring entity (wrong position). After every placement, re-read the entity with get_entity(proto, pos) and build at explicit coordinates. 2) An electric drill dropping straight into an electric furnace is the simplest smelting setup: 30 plates/min per pair with no fuel. 3) Electric furnaces and machines leave only the boiler needing coal. Feed it with a short belt from coal drills plus a burner inserter, which refuels itself from the coal it carries. 4) Inserters keep only about 5–12 coal in the boiler. After a reset that buffer is small, so keep the coal belt short and add a second feed. 5) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole sometimes reports success but leaves the target unpowered. Check the warnings and, if needed, place a pole by hand next to the entity. 6) The 800-unit output chest fills up and throughput then drops to 0. Chain a second chest through an inserter for buffer. 7) Two steam engines give a hard 1.8 MW cap, and you only have 2. Plan electric drills (90 kW), furnaces (180 kW) and assembling-machine-2 units (150 kW) to fit under it.\n\n[L3p1:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.4/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic, electric factory for automation science packs. It makes 22–23 packs per 60 s against a quota of 16 (checked over 60 s in step 18). Power: an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds one boiler at (-5,4.5), which drives two steam engines (the second joined by a single pipe at (3.5,8.5)). The boiler's coal is automated: an electric drill on the coal patch at (17.5,4.5) feeds a belt to an inserter that loads the boiler. Its fuel stays at about 5 coal and the belt stays full of spare coal. Iron: 2 electric drills at (17.5/20.5, 72.5) drop straight into 2 electric furnaces. Inserters put the plates on a belt that runs to the gear assembler. Copper: the same setup with 2 drills\nУроки головы: 1) Check the starting inventory first. Here it had electric furnaces and AM2, so the only coal consumer was the boiler, which removed most of the fuel-logistics work. 2) connect_entities with belts does not join two separate segments at a corner: the end belt keeps its old direction. Turn the corner belt with rotate_entity, or place belts one by one with an explicit direction. 3) Inserter direction in place_entity is the drop direction (LEFT means it drops to the left). Check pickup_position and drop_position after placing. 4) An inserter feeding a boiler shows WAITING_FOR_SPACE_IN_DESTINATION and a warning about an item on the ground, yet it still works: it only tops the boiler up to about 5 coal. Judge it by the fuel level over time, not by its status. 5) connect_entities with poles leaves relay poles in random places (one blocked a planned assembler spot), and it does not always cover the target, which gave NO_POWER. Place extra poles by hand and check statuses after about 20 s. 6) Direct insertion works well and saves belts: drill into furnace, and gear AM into pack AM through an inserter. 7) Two AM2s actually gave 16 per minute, not the theoretical 18. Leave at least a 30% margin; a third assembler raised output to 23. 8) Plan the layout ahead and use can_place_entity to scan for occupied tiles; get_entities with a radius is unreliable for checking whether something sits at an exact spot.\n\n[L3p1:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 35.1/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully automatic electric factory for logistic science packs. It reached 28 packs/min against a quota of 16, and the last two steps were steady at 28.\n\nPower: 2 offshore pumps, 2 boilers and 4 steam engines (3.6 MW). The second pair of engines was hand-crafted from iron plates I took out of a furnace. Coal comes from 3 electric drills on belts, with an inserter feeding each boiler. The second boiler takes its water through a pipe from the first boiler's spare water connection.\n\nOre: 5 iron and 2 copper electric drills, each dropping straight into an electric furnace. An inserter moves the plates onto an iron belt and a copper belt.\n\nAssembly (10 assembling-machine-2): one row has ca\nУроки головы: 1) For inserters, place_entity's direction is the drop direction (RIGHT means pick from the west, drop to the east). Placing belts tile by tile with explicit directions is predictable; connect_entities belts can wander (117 tiles for a ~20-tile gap) and wall off the area.\n2) connect_entities with MediumElectricPole often stops short and leaves gaps over 9 tiles. List the electricity-groups after each build and fill gaps with poles by hand; every steam engine needs pole coverage of its own.\n3) Electric drill → electric furnace placed at drill.drop_position → output inserter → belt is a simple ore-to-plate line that needs no fuel.\n4) The starting 2 engines (1.8 MW) are not enough for about 8 AM2, 6 electric furnaces and 8 drills. Everything slows down (LOW_POWER). Extra steam engines can be crafted from plates taken out of a furnace (craft_item handles the intermediate items).\n5) Keep one item type per belt (or per lane) and pass parts directly between assemblers with inserters, so overproduction can't block the line.\n6) getattr and imports are forbidden. Use plain attributes such as .belts, .poles, .inventory and .furnace_result.\n7) A pipe from a boiler's second water connection can feed a second boiler, which avoids having to route water from a new offshore pump.\n\n[L3p2:automation_science_pack_throughput] задача automation_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 26.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric automation-science-pack factory, and it holds at 22–23 packs/min against a quota of 16.\n- **Power:** an offshore pump at (-9.5,70.5) sends water about 75 tiles by pipe to one boiler at (17.5,1), which drives 2 steam engines. Two electric drills on the coal patch drop coal straight into the boiler, so no inserter is needed and the boiler stays at 50 coal.\n- **Iron:** 2 electric drills at y=72.5 each drop ore into an electric furnace. Inserters move plates from both furnaces directly into a gear AM2 at (22.5,69.5). Its output inserter puts gears on a belt at y=66.5 running west.\n- **Copper:** at the copper patch, 2 drills feed one electric furnace at (-48.5,69.5) from \nУроки головы: 1. nearest() searches from the player's current position. After move_to, nearest(Water) found a different lake, and the pipe became about 75 tiles long. Record resource coordinates before moving around.\n2. An electric drill can drop coal directly into a boiler, with no belt or inserter. Two drills on two sides of one boiler are a reliable fuel supply.\n3. Placing underground belts with place_entity: the first placement creates the input. Placing the second piece with Direction.LEFT at the exit tile gave an output facing RIGHT, connected to the input. connect_entities with UndergroundBelt failed to find a path.\n4. Every placement must be within 10 tiles of the player. The player_location variable goes stale, so call move_to explicitly every few tiles in a loop.\n5. connect_entities with MediumElectricPole can build a separate grid with voltage=0. A manual line of poles every 8 tiles is more reliable; afterwards check every entity for NO_POWER.\n6. An electric drill can't be placed where there is no ore under it. On the patch edge, place drills on the tiles that have ore.\n7. Iron and gears with direct insertion between furnace, gear AM2 and furnace work well. A gear belt and a copper belt on either side of a row of AM2s feed several science assemblers easily. 3 AM2s give about 21–23 packs/min, below the theoretical 27.\n\n[L3p2:electronic_circuit_throughput] задача electronic_circuit_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 24.8/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric, automatic electronic-circuit factory that holds a steady 22–23 circuits/min against a quota of 16. The first reading of 53 counted a buffer that had built up. Power: offshore pump, boiler and 2 steam engines near the water at (-9.5,1.5). The boiler gets coal from 2 electric drills facing each other at (18.5,-0.5) and (18.5,3.5), then a 24-tile belt along y=1.5, then a burner inserter at (-4.5,2.5). The boiler held 5–7 coal over time. Iron: 1 electric drill at (17.5,72.5) drops straight into an electric furnace at (14.5,72.5). An inserter moves the plates into the circuit AM2 at (10.5,72.5). Copper: 2 drills face each other into a furnace at (-48.5,74.5). An inserter\nУроки головы: 1) In this version (Factorio 2.0) the electric furnace is 3x3, not 2x2. Check footprints after placement with tile_dimensions, or the next machine ends up flush against it with no room for an inserter. 2) Two drills facing each other into one 3x3 furnace work vertically: a DOWN drill at y and an UP drill at y+6, with the furnace at y+3. 3) A long belt between ore patches can run into water. Get the lake's bounding box with get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, pos) and route around it tile by tile, wrapping each place in try/except. can_place_entity returns False beyond the player's reach, so it is useless for scanning a map remotely. 4) A medium pole's coverage reaches about 3.5 tiles. An inserter exactly 4 tiles away ends up NO_POWER, so check every inserter. connect_entities with MediumElectricPole connected areas 70 tiles apart without trouble. 5) Assembler to assembler for cable: a basic inserter moves about 0.83 items/s, so put 2 inserters in parallel (3 cables per circuit). 6) One electric furnace on copper caps output at about 25 circuits/min, and steady-state measured 22–23. This gives margin over 16; for more, add a second copper furnace. 7) The first throughput reading is inflated by the buffer (53 vs a real 23); measure again after 60 s.\n\n[L3p2:inserter_throughput] задача inserter_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 36.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric inserter factory. It held 30 inserters/min against a quota of 16, and the last two checks agreed.\n\nPower: an offshore pump at the lake (-9.5,1.5) feeds 2 boilers. The second boiler takes water from a single pipe on the first boiler's free water port. Together they drive 4 steam engines in a chain, 3.6 MW in total. Coal comes from 2 electric drills on the coal patch, down a belt to burner inserters on each boiler, and each boiler held 5–7 coal.\n\nIron: 4 electric drills, each with an electric furnace placed at its drop point. Inserters put the plates onto a belt at y=81.5.\n\nCopper: 2 drill-and-furnace pairs at x≈-50. Their belt has to go north around a lake at x -21..-\nУроки головы: 1. Count power for the steady state, with every machine working at once. 7–8 drills, 5–6 electric furnaces, 4 AM2 and about 15 inserters is more than 1.8 MW, so you need a second boiler and 4 engines. The second boiler can sit right below the first and share its water through one pipe on the free port. Engines can be chained in series through their steam connections.\n2. You can't hand-craft steam engines from iron plates, because the gear step needs a crafting machine. Take gears straight out of the gear AM2 with extract_item, plus plates from the furnaces, and then craft_item(SteamEngine) works. A boiler crafts from a stone furnace and pipes in the inventory.\n3. Before laying a long belt between ore patches, check for lakes with get_resource_patch(Resource.Water, midpoint, radius=30). place_entity fails on water, and the pole line breaks there too. A loop of single belt tiles plus a chain of poles placed by hand around the lake works.\n4. can_place_entity returns False far from the player, so don't use it to map terrain at a distance.\n5. The output chest fills within a few steps, because the harness runs simulated time between steps. Chain 2–3 chests with inserters.\n6. A drill facing a furnace, with the furnace's output inserter dropping onto a shared belt, is a reliable iron or copper line at about 30 plates/min. Placing the assemblers right along the belt, with parts passed between them by inserters, worked on the first try.\n7. get_entities() also returns groups (electricit\n\n[L3p2:iron_gear_wheel_throughput] задача iron_gear_wheel_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 37.2/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric iron-gear-wheel factory and finished in 9 of 20 steps. The last measurement was 32 gears/min and the best was 35, against a quota of 16.\n\nPower: offshore pump at (-9.5,-0.5), piped to a boiler at (20.5,6). The boiler sits right at the drop position of an electric coal drill at (20.5,8.5), so the drill feeds coal straight into it and it stayed at 50 coal. Two steam engines are stacked above the boiler, giving 1.8 MW against roughly 0.85 MW of load.\n\nProduction: two electric drills on iron ore at (20.5,80.5) and (28.5,80.5), each dropping into an electric furnace placed with place_entity_next_to(UP). An inserter takes plates from each furnace into an AM2 set to gears a\nУроки головы: 1. Put the boiler right at an electric coal drill's drop position (place_entity_next_to(Boiler, drill.position, UP)) and the drill feeds coal straight into it. No belt or inserter is needed, and the boiler stayed at 50 coal.\n2. Stack steam engines with place_entity_next_to(SteamEngine, prev.position, UP). The second engine needs its own pole nearby, or it shows NOT_PLUGGED_IN_ELECTRIC_NETWORK.\n3. connect_entities(Pump, Boiler, Pipe) over 30+ tiles worked on the first try.\n4. A long connect_entities line with MediumElectricPole left a gap of about 11 tiles at the end, and the factory's poles formed a separate group with voltage 0. Always check that only one ElectricityGroup exists and close gaps by hand; wire reach is about 9 tiles.\n5. A compact layout works well: drill, then electric furnace at the drop position, inserter, AM2, inserter, second furnace and drill. Place everything by explicit coordinates and print pickup and drop positions.\n6. A wooden chest holds 1600 gears (16 stacks of 100), not 800. For a 45-minute run at about 35/min, chain three or four chests with inserters.\n7. Don't spend a whole step only gathering information. Combine the resource-patch survey with the first build.\n\n[L3p2:iron_plate_throughput] задача iron_plate_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 74.5/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built an all-electric iron-plate factory in 7 steps. On the power side, an offshore pump at (-9.5,1.5) feeds one boiler at (-5,4.5), which drives two steam engines at (0.5,8.5) and (5.5,8.5); both engines show WORKING. The boiler gets coal automatically: an electric drill on the coal patch at (17.5,4.5) drops onto a straight belt laid west one tile at a time, about 19 tiles to (-2.5,4.5). From there a burner inserter at (-3.5,4.5) loads the boiler and refuels itself from the belt. The boiler held about 6 coal. Smelting is on the iron patch about 70 tiles south, reached by a line of medium poles from (15.5,6.5) via connect_entities. It has two identical units at x=20.5 and x=26.5. Each unit\nУроки головы: 1. An electric drill facing UP with place_entity_next_to(ElectricFurnace, drill.position, UP) puts the furnace right on the drop position. After that, place_entity_next_to(Inserter, furnace.position, UP) gave the correct pickup and drop with no rotation needed. 2. nearest_buildable with a BuildingBox placed the boiler and engine on the first try, and connect_entities(Pipe) linked the pump, boiler and engine. A second engine via place_entity_next_to(SteamEngine, eng.position, RIGHT, spacing=0) picked up steam by itself. 3. Laying belts one tile at a time with an explicit direction and a move_to every few tiles was reliable over about 19 tiles. 4. connect_entities with MediumElectricPole from one pole position to another pole worked over about 70 tiles with no gaps. Placing poles yourself in a free column between two units covers both. 5. One electric drill plus one electric furnace gives about 30 plates/min, so two units leave a big margin over a quota of 16. 6. The boiler's burner inserter reporting WAITING_FOR_SPACE with an 'item on the ground' warning is normal. Judge it by the boiler's fuel level instead.\n\n[L3p2:logistics_science_pack_throughput] задача logistics_science_pack_throughput: результат игры — УСПЕХ, выпуск после 45 мин без агента 29.2/мин (квота 16)\nЧто построили: I built a fully electric logistic-science-pack factory. Measured throughput was 22-23 per minute against a quota of 16; the best reading was 23.\nPower: one offshore pump feeds 2 boilers and 4 steam engines (3.6 MW). I crafted the 2 extra engines from plates taken out of the iron furnaces. Three electric drills on coal fill one belt, and a burner inserter from that belt feeds each boiler.\nRaw materials: 5 iron drills and 2 copper drills each drop straight into an electric furnace (3x3). Inserters move the plates onto belts that run to the assembly area: about 150 iron and 60 copper per minute.\nAssembly line, all AM2, linked by direct insertion: cables, then circuits (two inserters between the\nУроки головы: 1. The electric furnace is 3x3, not 2x2. A drill, furnace and inserter column has a 3-tile pitch: drill y=72.5 facing UP, furnace y=69.5, inserter y=67.5, belt y=66.5.\n2. can_place_entity returns False when the character is too far away, even if the spot is free. move_to the spot first. Simplest is to call place_entity inside try/except and then check the result with get_entity.\n3. place_entity and place_entity_next_to sometimes return a stale object, so a later piece ended up at a wrong spot (an extra copper furnace appeared at x=-7.5). Build only by explicit coordinates and check each piece with get_entity.\n4. A boiler placed with direction LEFT stands vertically: water points at (x+0.5, y±2), steam output at (x-1.5, y). A second boiler can draw water from the first pump's existing water pipe group.\n5. If the inventory has only 2 engines, a steam engine is crafted from about 26 plates plus pipes. extract_item takes the plates from furnaces that are FULL_OUTPUT. A second power block raised throughput from 14-15 (LOW_POWER) to 18.\n6. Keep inserters and transport belts on separate belts, on opposite sides of the science assemblers, so the line never jams. A second output inserter on the inserter assembler feeds a fourth science assembler: 18 -> 23.\n7. Do not print every belt with get_entities: the output overflows. Print only problem statuses, plus belt groups and boiler fuel.\n8. The first belt range in a range() loop was one tile short, and the boiler went without coal. Check\n\nНапиши один полный свод правил. Предела длины нет: включи все правила, которые подтверждаются эпизодами и полезны агенту, — как действовать в этой среде, что работает, чего избегать, какие проверки делать, с конкретными приёмами и числами. Каждое правило — с меткой происхождения в квадратных скобках: id эпизода или свода и какую ошибку лечит. Противоречащее успехам — убери. Пиши общие правила для любых задач этой среды, не рецепт под одну задачу.\nВерни: rules — текст свода; words — число слов."
const S = {"type": "object", "properties": {"rules": {"type": "string"}, "words": {"type": "number"}}, "required": ["rules", "words"]}
